.TH tuseq n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuseq
.PP
\fBseq\fR\-like numeric sequence generation in pure Tcl.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tuseq::range ?first? ?incr? last ?options?
::tclutils::tuseq::text  ?first? ?incr? last ?options?
.CE
.PP
Positional forms: \fBlast\fR, \fBfirst last\fR, or \fBfirst incr last\fR (negative steps allowed). Options: \fB\-separator S\fR (text only, default newline), \fB\-format F\fR (printf format), \fB\-equalwidth 0|1\fR (pad numbers with leading zeros to equal width).
.PP
Options may stand before, between or after the values. An argument that starts with \fB\-\fR and is not a number starts an option; negative numbers are values. \fBrange\fR rejects \fB\-separator\fR as an unknown option.
.PP
When all three values are integers (of any size, also 64\-bit values under Tcl 8.6), the sequence is computed with integers; otherwise with doubles, formatted with \fB%g\fR.
.CS
::tclutils::tuseq::text 3 -separator ,          ;# -> 1,2,3
::tclutils::tuseq::range 5000000000 5000000001  ;# -> 5000000000 5000000001
.CE
.SS Errors
.TS
l l.
Case	\fB\-errorcode\fR
no value or more than three	\fB{TCLUTILS TUSEQ ARGS}\fR
value is not a number	\fB{TCLUTILS TUSEQ VALUE}\fR
increment 0	\fB{TCLUTILS TUSEQ INCREMENT}\fR
option without value	\fB{TCLUTILS TUSEQ OPTION}\fR
unknown option (also \fB\-separator\fR for \fBrange\fR)	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION \-name}\fR
.TE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tuseq.tcl 1 2 10
tclsh bin/tuseq.tcl -equalwidth 1 8 11
.CE
